+## UBU-D0350: Interruptions require scoped permission while service stops preserve eligibility
+
+**Status:** Accepted → DESIGN.md §21.1.7. Resolves `UBU-Q0078`; consolidates `UBU-D0201`/`UBU-D0272` with `UBU-D0309`–`UBU-D0311`, `UBU-D0325`–`UBU-D0328`, `UBU-D0330` and `UBU-D0339`.
+
+For Phase 2, distinguish interaction mode, processing route, attention and Compartment. Capture is explicit, finite, source/purpose/Device-bound and independently controllable from speech. Meeting/cloud selections remain unavailable until their separate gates pass; restart, sync and handoff convey no live consent.
+
+Unsolicited realtime/discovery alerts default off. User-enabled rules bind conditions, permitted evidence, freshness, channels, quiet/suppression behavior and finite aggregate limits. Deadline risk, current-work blockers, material external events and requested monitoring may prompt under those rules; affect inference alone cannot. Clarification stays within the current request or enabled rule and remaining budget.
+
+Invalid eligibility stops the affected UbU service regardless of alert settings. Professional/urgent guidance stops retain §21.1.6's allowed output and authority limits. Notices and repair proposals admit no state or external action and cannot override silence, privacy or restricted attention.
+
+Coalesce condition episodes, persist dismissal/snooze/disable choices and never escalate from nonresponse. Record minimized overrides through existing counterfactual decision events with optional reasons and no Preference inference. Calibration proposes explicitly accepted interaction-setting changes without expanding capture or optimizing compliance.
+
+DESIGN.md §21.1.7 specifies visible status and behavioral enablement fixtures. This resolves the product policy, not implementation acceptance, numerical attention/timing profiles or additional capture scope.
